data: {"entry": {"lap": 3, "stage": "convergence", "message": "Infeasible design on lap 3: The spiral closes at MTOW 3,484 kg, above the 2,722 kg limit for a single-engine piston aircraft (FAA AC 23.1309-1E, Class I (single reciprocating engine, under 6,000 lb)). The statistical methods don't apply that far out.", "citations": ["Raymer 2ed, Ch. 3 (p. 22)", "Raymer 2ed, Eq. 3.11 (p. 23)", "Raymer 2ed, Eq. 3.4 (p. 12)", "Raymer 2ed, Eq. 3.6 (p. 17)", "Raymer 2ed, Eq. 3.8 (p. 17)", "Raymer 2ed, Eq. 5.2 (p. 81)", "Raymer 2ed, Eq. 5.6 (p. 85)", "Raymer 2ed, Table 3.1 (p. 13)", "Raymer 2ed, Table 3.2 (p. 16)", "Raymer 2ed, Table 3.4 (p. 19)", "Raymer 2ed, Table 5.2 (p. 79)", "Raymer 2ed, Fig. 14.10 (p. 343): Schrenk's approximation", "knowledge/equations.yaml#schrenk_lift_distribution", "Derived from Raymer 2ed, Eqs. 14.35-14.36 (pp. 383-384) for an idealised two-cap beam", "Raymer 2ed, Eq. 14.35 (p. 383)", "Raymer 2ed, Eq. 14.36 (p. 384)", "Raymer 2ed, Eq. 14.37 (p. 385)", "Raymer 2ed, Ch. 14 (p. 385): caps carry bending, web carries shear", "Converted to SI from Raymer 2ed, Table 14.3 (p. 366), row Clad 2024 extrusions", "knowledge/tables/materials.yaml#al_2024_t3", "Raymer 6ed, Table 6.3 (Fuselage Length Regression)", "Raymer 6ed, Table 6.4 (Tail Volume Coefficients C_HT=0.70, C_VT=0.04)", "knowledge/tables/aircraft_typical.yaml#ga_single_engine"], "level": "error", "timestamp": "2026-10-31T14:00:44+00:00"}}

