data: {"entry": {"lap": 3, "stage": "convergence", "message": "Proposed change: The spiral closes at MTOW 3,484 kg, above the 2,722 kg limit for a single-engine piston aircraft (FAA AC 23.1309-1E, Class I (single reciprocating engine, under 6,000 lb)). The statistical methods don't apply that far out. Keeping everything else in the spec, the longest range that closes is 4,660 km (down from 5,570 km), where the spiral converges at 2,720 kg. Both numbers come from re-running the full spiral at the new range.", "citations": ["Spiral re-run at the proposed value (bisection on range)"], "level": "warning", "timestamp": "2026-10-31T14:00:45+00:00"}}

